ere apostrophe is actually U+2019, not U+0027)\r\n  2. Ensure spellchecker is on and `spelllang` is some dialect of English.\r\n\r\nObserved:\r\n    ![Snímek z 2019-03-25 08-01-24](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/198999/54907126-164af800-4ee5-11e9-9477-00a517346e15.png)\r\nThe phrase \"hasn’t\" is marked as spelling error.\r\n\r\nExpected:\r\n    It is not a spelling error. vim should replace all curly characters(“ ” „ ‘ ’ ‚) with their pure ASCII equivalents to avoid confusing spellchecker, or something. Obviously change of dictionaries is not a proper solution, because spellchecking is done on many files where keeping the file plain ASCII is completely correct behaviour (programming source code).\r\n\r\nThis is another take on the problem described in #3747 and of course fixing finally #846 would be also a solution.\r\n\r\nOf course, fixing #356 would help as well.\r\n\r\nOriginally, filed as https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/9784 but I got sent here because it is completely shared issue between vim and neovim.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vim/vim/issues/4168/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vim/vim/issues/4168/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/476110708","html_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/9784#issuecomment-476110708","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/9784","id":476110708,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3NjExMDcwOA==","user":{"login":"mcepl","id":198999,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODk5OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198999?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcepl","html_url":"https://github.com/mcepl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcepl/followers","following_url":"https://ap